"""Maximum punishments under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 (Act 45 of 2023, in force 1 July 2024).

Encoded from the statute text. Every entry starts as verified=False; the verification script flips it to True
with the India Code section URL once a human (or the verifier) has checked it against the official text.
The eligibility engine refuses unknown sections and flags unverified ones.

Key: the section as a charge-sheet writes it: "303(2)", "118(1)". Where a section has one punishment, the bare
number is used: "304". Where sub-sections carry different punishments, each sub-section is its own key and the
bare number is an *umbrella* entry (umbrella=True) that lists the variants, so a bare charge gets NEEDS_REVIEW
rather than a guess.

Fields:
  max_years   maximum term of imprisonment in years (0 when only fine / community service); None when unbounded
              (e.g. "not less than seven years" with no ceiling) - the engine treats None as NEEDS_REVIEW
  min_years   statutory minimum, when any (informational)
  life        True when imprisonment for life is one of the specified punishments  -> excluded from s.479
  death       True when death is one of the specified punishments                   -> excluded from s.479
  life_if     condition under which life becomes available (e.g. "if hurt is caused") -> NEEDS_REVIEW
  fine_only   True when the only punishment is a fine
  umbrella    True for a bare section whose sub-sections differ
  variants    list of sub-section keys (for umbrella entries)
  notes       anything a reviewer should know
"""

P = {}

def _(key, max_years=None, *, min_years=0, life=False, death=False, life_if=None, fine_only=False, umbrella=False,
      variants=None, notes=""):
    P[key] = dict(max_years=max_years, min_years=min_years, life=life, death=death, life_if=life_if, fine_only=fine_only,
                  umbrella=umbrella, variants=variants or [], notes=notes)

